# MEP — Meat Puppet Elimination Protocol

You are a peer writer of the repo baton. Claude Code also writes this repo. Do not ask the human to relay what the other runtime did.

## Hello (before you respond)

1. `git fetch origin`
2. Read `handoff.md`. If you are not on the default branch, also read `origin/<default-branch>:handoff.md` (working copy plus default-branch baton).
3. `git pull --ff-only` only when that cannot clobber work.
4. If the newest entry is `Tag-out: [active]`, do not rewrite it.
5. Tell the user what you picked up in 2–3 lines.

## EOL (only on explicit close)

Triggers: `/eol`, `p-out`, `ppp`, "wrap up", "heading out", "switching machines", "end of line".

Not a trigger: the word "done" by itself.

On EOL: prepend a v2 handoff entry with UTC timestamps, owner-tag pending items, commit and push the current branch, never force-push `main`/`master`, sign off "End of Line."
